WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.540
Authorization decides what the authenticated subject may access or do.

2
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:13.960
Roles, permissions, scopes, and claims can all help express capability, but sensitive APIs usually need more context.

3
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:19.820
The service should verify the current subject, action, resource, and context.

4
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:32.240
Context may include tenant, organization, ownership, workflow state, delegated access, risk level, and whether the request is user-initiated or service-initiated.

5
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.520
Object-level authorization is one of the most important API controls.

6
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:43.340
A caller being allowed to use an endpoint does not mean the caller can access every record referenced by that endpoint.

7
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.760
List endpoints should filter results to what the caller may see.

8
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.460
Detail endpoints should check access to the specific object.

9
00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:58.280
Update, delete, export, and administrative actions should verify permission at the point where the operation occurs.

10
00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.560
Tenant and organization boundaries deserve special attention.

11
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:09.140
Multi-tenant APIs should prevent one tenant from reading, modifying, exporting, or triggering work against another tenant's data.

12
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.600
This cannot be left to client behavior, hidden buttons, hidden routes, or documentation.

13
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:21.580
Server-side enforcement should be present even when the caller is internal, privileged, or using an integration path.

14
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.040
Boundaries should be testable and visible during review.

15
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.800
Delegated access and administrative actions should be narrow and auditable.

16
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:41.100
Support tools, background services, partner integrations, and admin endpoints often need special privileges, but those privileges should be explicit, limited, and logged.

17
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.040
A mature API does not ask only whether a subject is powerful.

18
00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:51.380
It asks whether this subject is allowed to perform this action on this resource for this reason right now.
